00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
The SpongeBob Movie: Search for SquarePants is a 2025 American animated adventure comedy film
based on the SpongeBob SquarePants television series, created by Stephen Hillenburg.

15
00:46:36,428 --> 00:46:42,428
Directed by series veteran Derek Drymon, it stars the show's regular voice cast alongside
George Lopez, Ice Spice, Arturo Castro, Sherry Cola, Regina Hall, and Mark Hamill.

16
00:49:42,857 --> 00:49:48,857
The plot follows SpongeBob on a quest to prove his bravery by adventuring with
the ghost pirate, The Flying Dutchman, through the Underworld.

17
00:52:49,285 --> 00:52:55,285
It is the fourth theatrical film based on the series, following
2020's Sponge on the Run, and the sixth film overall.

18
00:55:55,714 --> 00:56:01,714
The film was written by Pam Brady and Matt Lieberman, from a story by
Brady and series creatives Marc Ceccarelli and Kaz.

19
00:59:02,142 --> 00:59:08,142
It was first developed as a direct-to-streaming film focused on Mr.

20
01:02:08,571 --> 01:02:14,571
Krabs, but the project was later retooled into a theatrical
feature with SpongeBob as the lead character instead.

21
01:05:14,999 --> 01:05:20,999
By April 2023, Drymon had been hired to direct the film.

22
01:08:21,428 --> 01:08:27,428
In July 2024, Hamill was revealed to be voicing the Flying
Dutchman in the film in place of Brian Doyle-Murray.

23
01:11:27,857 --> 01:11:33,857
John Debney composed the film's score, after having
previously scored 2015's Sponge Out of Water.

24
01:14:34,285 --> 01:14:40,285
Search for SquarePants premiered at the AFI Film Festival on October 26, 2025, before holding a premiere in New York City
on December 17, and was theatrically released by Paramount Pictures in the United States on December 19.

25
01:17:40,714 --> 01:17:46,714
The film received mostly positive reviews from critics
and has grossed $153.5 million worldwide.

26
